{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset","id":1507439,"title":"(Immaculate Area) How much can gods & mortals interact without DB / IM geting upset?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-04T17:03:50-07:00","id":1507439,"title":"(Immaculate Area) How much can gods & mortals interact without DB / IM geting upset?","content":"This primarily related to a character's backstory but how does gods and mortals interaction go in an immaculate heavy area (such as Lookshy or the Realm)?<br /> <br /> Can a god appear before a mortal praying at their temple and give guidance/training/gifts? (Without an immaculate monk getting upset?)<br /> <br /> Can a god testify on a mortal's behalf in a trial etc (They didn't do the crime officer etc) if they chose?<br /> <br /> Would they have to act through a Immaculate Monk intermediary? Would the Monk take it seriously? <br /> <br /> To be a bit more specific, in Lookshy could Tien-yu or Tu-yu show up and guide a mortal soldier/helot/student ? Without the Dragon Blooded getting upset and maybe the Dragon-blooded listening to the god if they spoke on the mortals behalf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T01:10:50-07:00","id":1507462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset#post1507439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This primarily related to a character's backstory but how does gods and mortals interaction go in an immaculate heavy area (such as Lookshy or the Realm)?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> My first impulse is to answer &quot;it depends&quot;, as not all parts of the Blessed Isle or even Lookshy's territory are equal, so degree of Immaculate emphasis on certain practices, local deities, leading dynasts, patrician families, major temples or pilgrimage routes among other things may lead to a considerable degree of regional variation in practice from place to place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset#post1507439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a god appear before a mortal praying at their temple and give guidance/training/gifts? (Without an immaculate monk getting upset?)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Well, it could but why would it if charms like Dreamscape cost less motes while offers greater discretion and safety on plausible deniability?<br /> <br /> (Supposing we are speaking of a celestial or terrestial spirit, that is - an elemental, that already exists in a material state on principle might find physically appearing to a worshipper more convenient in place of projecting its image, voice or whatever instead)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset#post1507439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a god testify on a mortal's behalf in a trial etc (They didn't do the crime officer etc) if they chose?<br /> <br /> Would they have to act through a Immaculate Monk intermediary? Would the Monk take it seriously?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's hypothetically possible, though a mightly disruptive way of going at things - though more importantly, what is the deity's reputation and motives to do so?<br /> <br /> People might have the deepest respect for Zeus and even swear oaths in his name, but how many would not trust him as witness in a tribunal hearing, specially if a pretty woman is involved in some way? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Plus, are there not less obstrusive or straighforward ways - like cursing and tormenting the acual guilty parts with nightmares, diseases, bad luck among a bunch of other things until confession - that a deity could interneve on the matter?\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset#post1507439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be a bit more specific, in Lookshy could Tien-yu or Tu-yu show up and guide a mortal soldier/helot/student ? Without the Dragon Blooded getting upset and maybe the Dragon-blooded listening to the god if they spoke on the mortals behalf?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> More specific details could be helpful there - just by your example, while related Tien-yu and Tu-yu are wildly different deities in matters of power, interests, attitudes and <i>degree of sanity</i> even, so i'd say that circunstances and people involved can matter a lot. I honestly can see a Sohei being <i>honestly worried for the poor mortal's physical or spiritual wellbeing</i> depending on what one knows or not.<br /> <br /> A person under <i>Tien-yu</i>'s wing could be a budding hero, the key cat's paw/neccessary sacrifice at the right moment in a crucial future conflict of the 7th Legion or both things even.<br /> <br /> Now being taken under the tutelage of <i><b>Tu-yu</b></i>, an eccentric deity living on nostalgia of the shogunate and of questionable influence or even purchase on reality..... oh boy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-02-2024, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T17:42:18-07:00","id":1507632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1507462#post1507462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Well, it could but why would it if charms like Dreamscape cost less motes while offers greater discretion and safety on plausible deniability?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if I remember that one. Did a quick search in the core but couldn't find it. Could you tell me which book please?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1507462#post1507462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say it's hypothetically possible, though a mightly disruptive way of going at things - though more importantly, what is the deity's reputation and motives to do so?<br /> <br /> People might have the deepest respect for Zeus and even swear oaths in his name, but how many would not trust him as witness in a tribunal hearing, specially if a pretty woman is involved in some way? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Plus, are there not less obstrusive or straighforward ways - like cursing and tormenting the acual guilty parts with nightmares, diseases, bad luck among a bunch of other things until confession - that a deity could interneve on the matter?\u200b<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well this is more in the way of protecting the 'innocent' on trial.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1507462#post1507462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More specific details could be helpful there - just by your example, while related Tien-yu and Tu-yu are wildly different deities in matters of power, interests, attitudes and <i>degree of sanity</i> even, so i'd say that circunstances and people involved can matter a lot. I honestly can see a Sohei being <i>honestly worried for the poor mortal's physical or spiritual wellbeing</i> depending on what one knows or not.<br /> <br /> A person under <i>Tien-yu</i>'s wing could be a budding hero, the key cat's paw-neccessary sacrifice at the right moment in a crucial future conflict of the 7th Legion or both things even.<br /> <br /> Now being taken under the tutelage of <i><b>Tu-yu</b></i>, an eccentric deity living on nostalgia of the shogunate and of questionable influence or even purchase on reality..... oh boy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Person involved is a young god-blood or beastman (actually something else but that is what he looks like.) in Lookshy's academy.<br /> <br /> It's a bit of back-story for a character: Orphan, raised in Lookshy, given guidance by Tien-yu / Tu-yu (not necessarily aware that he is being favored or by whom). Boy enrolls in military academy but is about to be court-martialed and executed (or exiled if certain dieties speak for him.) <br /> <br /> I just want to know how likely that is. Would having a Monk be the go-between be better?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T17:59:06-07:00","id":1507634,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure there is a &quot;canon&quot; answer to that question, so my recommendation is to think about what works better for your game and your table of players. Personally, I like a fairly high level of supernatural activity (elemental, spirits, etc.) in my game, so I definitely think a god's assistance sounds more fun than a monk's. But your table might be the exact opposite. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T03:31:21-07:00","id":1507679,"title":"","content":"The Immaculates doesn't believe human-god interactions are always wrong, but that they are potentially dangerous and shouldn't happen without some form of Immaculate oversight. But the nature of the oversight can be variable. Gods that help the Immaculates with tasks they considers important are given more leeway. At least one god was allowed to make an Exigent, which is a pretty extreme form of god-mortal interaction. So anything less than that is certainly possible for a favored god. <br /> <br /> Probably in Lookshy Tien-yu and Tu-yu are on pretty friendly terms with the Immaculate Faith so I think they could be allowed to do something like that, though maybe guiding a helot would be seen as disrupting the Perfected Hierarchy and thus potentially problematic (although maybe the Immaculate Faith - Immaculate Order differences means that members of the Immaculate Faith don't believe the helot's status is a religious matter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T22:55:12-07:00","id":1507742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1507632#post1507632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure if I remember that one. Did a quick search in the core but couldn't find it. Could you tell me which book please?</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, too used to having the previous editions for reference - not sure if Dreamscape has already been updated and ported to 3e yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1507632#post1507632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWell this is more in the way of protecting the 'innocent' on trial.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Well, as long as it's not some sort of institutional conspiracy out to ruin the PC - and he IS truly innocent - &quot;finding the guilty party, intimidating it into confessing through supernatural displays&quot; is something that should definitely work. Anyway, &quot;poping up on trial&quot; seems like an almost too late and not very practical way of solving things when one is a spirit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TryingToBeSlim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1507632#post1507632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Person involved is a young god-blood or beastman (actually something else but that is what he looks like.) in Lookshy's academy.<br /> <br /> It's a bit of back-story for a character: Orphan, raised in Lookshy, given guidance by Tien-yu / Tu-yu (not necessarily aware that he is being favored or by whom). Boy enrolls in military academy but is about to be court-martialed and executed (or exiled if certain dieties speak for him.)<br /> <br /> I just want to know how likely that is. Would having a Monk be the go-between be better?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. Truth be told, the accused visibly being a god-blood or beastman actually makes the case <b>worse </b>for the deity imho, since it becomes easier to dismiss their motives as less than altruistic.<br /> <br /> Also, just to clear up things - you keep mentioning Tien-yu &amp; Tu-yu both, like you are not invested in either of them as patron for the PC and any deity as long as it's associated with Lookshy will do. Is that the case or do you have some particular reason to cite both?<br /> <br /> <br /> But the real big question is - what did the character actually do to be court-martialed and executed (specially considering that as a student he possibly wasn't even part of military yet) in the first place? And was he truly innocent or not?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T03:12:11-07:00","id":1507755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1507742#post1507742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as long as it's not some sort of institutional conspiracy out to ruin the PC - and he IS truly innocent - &quot;finding the guilty party, intimidating it into confessing through supernatural displays&quot; is something that should definitely work. Anyway, &quot;poping up on trial&quot; seems like an almost too late and not very practical way of solving things when one is a spirit.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the 'crime' happened on a Training Expedition which turned ugly and now they are back in Lookshy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1507742#post1507742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. Truth be told, the accused visibly being a god-blood or beastman actually makes the case <b>worse </b>for the deity imho, since it becomes easier to dismiss their motives as less than altruistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I should have been more clear: Character looks more like a Human-Dragon King hybrid. People just mistake him as either a Beastman (more likely) or God-Blooded (less likely but since the character can use essence a little...) <br /> <br /> That being said he looks nothing like either Tu-Yu or Tien-Yu<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1507742#post1507742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, just to clear up things - you keep mentioning Tien-yu &amp; Tu-yu both, like you are not invested in either of them as patron for the PC and any deity as long as it's associated with Lookshy will do. Is that the case or do you have some particular reason to cite both?</div> </div> </div> </div>In all honesty I am waffling a bit. I like both of them but in terms of age and knowing what the Character is I think it should be Tu-yu but in terms of actual interaction I lean towards Tien yu.<br /> <br /> So I do think Tien-yu would be more likely to make an appearence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1507742#post1507742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the real big question is - what did the character actually do to be court-martialed and executed (specially considering that as a student he possibly wasn't even part of military yet) in the first place? And was he truly innocent or not?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Crime was disobeying orders in combat situation, fairly guilty.<br /> <br /> On the other hand he did save some people/kids one of whom exalted as a DB later in the fight whom Lookshy wants to recruit. Note: The 'commander' was Teresu Gido (NPC from 2E Scroll of Exalts, HATES Spirits and God-Blooded.) and he deliberately gave 'BAD' orders to the suspected God-Blood to get him killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4678-tryingtobeslim","name":"TryingToBeSlim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-08T06:41:50-07:00","id":1507763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1507742#post1507742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My bad, too used to having the previous editions for reference - not sure if Dreamscape has already been updated and ported to 3e yet.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There might be a published god with a Charm to communicate with people in dreams, but there's no one-size-fits-all of that or any other spirit Charm (except Measure the Wind and Hurry Home) because that's not how spirits are being written anymore.<br /> <br /> Anyway, for the Immaculate Order, I think that while they have degrees of permissiveness for divine interventions depending on need and the appropriate conduct from the god, direct relationships with mortals are considered taboo across the board. Something as mundane as testifying in a trial would likely often be considered out of sorts.<br /> <br /> Nor would I think in the Realm there's much capacity to either call upon a monk at will to convey information, nor even really much provision to testify before a judge on behalf of an absent witness.<br /> <br /> I think Lookshy would be less severe about their presence by a bit (but still not wanting gods to feel like they can compete with Dragon-Blooded for social prominence in the city itself), but I'd still think testimony in trial would often be out of sorts. If it's significant, I think Tien-Yu would be more about using back channels to communicate certain intentions to the General Staff in a manner that comes back to ensure leniency in the sentencing even while finding a person guilty.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-09T12:23:14-07:00","id":1507886,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I\u2019ve always counted the relations as anything that would involve a deeper meaning requires the Immaculates. If Ahlat appeared on the holiday of cattle celebration, then I don\u2019t think the Immaculates would mind a prayer ceremony of Ahlat (let by themselves or an officially appointed Immaculate Priest of course), getting a small word of praise, or even showing Ahlat your prized bull with him then saying \u2018nice work.\u2019</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The issue for the Immaculate comes from anything that involves deeper meaning or thought. Ahlat asking \u201cwhat do you think this day means?\u201d to a follower would set off concern, while him giving advice on the logistics of cattle runs would be met with alarms, as it would be the duty of the Immaculates to ensure that the information given to the peasants meets with the Realms best inte- I mean suitably broken down so an untrained mind can process it.</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T17:29:53-07:00","id":1508089,"title":"","content":"My personal take is that the official party line of the Immaculate Faith re: the appropriate level of direct interaction between Gods and Mortals is &quot;none at all.&quot; When mediated by a terrestrial, especially an appropriate authority within the proper contexts, then okay.<br /> <br /> If a god decides to so much as say, &quot;hi.&quot; to a mortal, then they enter into theoretically actionable territory, much like someone going just a bit over the speed limit. There's probably a little leeway that individual Dragon-Blooded are allowed to exercise: Dynasts who have better things to do (whether distracted by their own cares or well-placed bribes) may be incredibly lax, while someone like Peleps Deled may brutally beat a god to nonexistence for even manifesting outside of pre-designated circumstances. <br /> <br /> So any god who decides to interact with a mortal just has to ask themselves, &quot;Do I feel lucky?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, do they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T22:46:24-07:00","id":1508115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1508089#post1508089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal take is that the official party line of the Immaculate Faith re: the appropriate level of direct interaction between Gods and Mortals is &quot;none at all.&quot; When mediated by a terrestrial, especially an appropriate authority within the proper contexts, then okay.<br /> <br /> If a god decides to so much as say, &quot;hi.&quot; to a mortal, then they enter into theoretically actionable territory, much like someone going just a bit over the speed limit. There's probably a little leeway that individual Dragon-Blooded are allowed to exercise: Dynasts who have better things to do (whether distracted by their own cares or well-placed bribes) may be incredibly lax, while someone like Peleps Deled may brutally beat a god to nonexistence for even manifesting outside of pre-designated circumstances.<br /> <br /> So any god who decides to interact with a mortal just has to ask themselves, &quot;Do I feel lucky?&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, do they?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Immaculate Faith is specifically Lookshy and maybe some other Shogunate holdouts. Dynasts follow the Immaculate Order, which regards the Faith as, at best, misguided, or at least has in prior editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T13:24:26-07:00","id":1508187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1508115#post1508115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Immaculate Faith is specifically Lookshy and maybe some other Shogunate holdouts. Dynasts follow the Immaculate Order, which regards the Faith as, at best, misguided, or at least has in prior editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, my mistake. I meant to refer to whatever beliefs lie at the root of both the Order and its Lookshy counterpart, but ended up referring directly to the latter. Bleh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T11:28:09-07:00","id":1508286,"title":"","content":"You know, I think that's a hard distinction that should be reserved for the books more than casual conversation where it can probably be generally understood what a person means.<br /> <br /> Much like how Charting Fate's Course includes a sidebar about the fact that the words &quot;fate&quot; and &quot;destiny&quot; get used by normal people, the majority of gods, and even the occasional Sidereal speaking colloquially or with poetic licence in ways other than their strict technical meaning to the Bureau of Destiny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T15:13:12-07:00","id":1508303,"title":"","content":"If I recall the official stance for the whole immaculate issue vis a vis gods interacting with mortals is that they're not supposed to. The whole DBs being the bridge between the divine and mortal and all that so technically they're supposed to get involved if the god is interacting with mortals outside of stuff ordained by clergy or DB authorization. <br /> <br /> In practice that's probably pretty commonly ignored so long as the god isn't doing anything to weaken the power the immaculates have or get themselves extra worship and so on. Especially if its an older tradition. Like no one is going to object if its just a long standing thing for the local harvest god to show up at one of the farms that had struggled the most to go, &quot;Okay, so here's what went wrong with your crops this year. This part here you couldn't have done anything about storm dragons aren't a thing you can prepare for. But here's what you can do to lessen the flooding that caused havoc to this field.&quot; Or if the island's forge goddess holds generational contests where the winner is granted the privilege of being an apprentice blacksmith under her. There is probably objections to say Ahlat training his own personal general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T20:47:46-07:00","id":1508325,"title":"","content":"And they can allow things as part of calendar negotiations. &quot;We can let the local farmers can keep singing their traditional work-hymns in the fields, but in that case you'll be allotted less worship in the harvest festivals. You can't have both.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26529-anshu","name":"Anshu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26529_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T07:14:45-07:00","id":1508354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1508115#post1508115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Immaculate Faith is specifically Lookshy and maybe some other Shogunate holdouts. Dynasts follow the Immaculate Order, which regards the Faith as, at best, misguided, or at least has in prior editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had thought (citation needed) that &quot;Immaculate Faith&quot; was the overall term for the DB-centric beliefs, and the Immaculate Order was specifically the monastic-organization/state-religion headed by the Mouth of Peace. Like, &quot;Christianity&quot; vs &quot;The Roman Catholic Church&quot;. Is it more &quot;Greater Vehicle&quot;/&quot;Lesser Vehicle&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-14T15:39:12-07:00","id":1508397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1507439-immaculate-area-how-much-can-gods-mortals-interact-without-db-im-geting-upset?p=1508354#post1508354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had thought (citation needed) that &quot;Immaculate Faith&quot; was the overall term for the DB-centric beliefs, and the Immaculate Order was specifically the monastic-organization/state-religion headed by the Mouth of Peace. Like, &quot;Christianity&quot; vs &quot;The Roman Catholic Church&quot;. Is it more &quot;Greater Vehicle&quot;/&quot;Lesser Vehicle&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever since Exalted: the Outcaste, &quot;Immaculate faith&quot; has been what Lookshy believes, specifically. &quot;Immaculate Philosophy&quot; might be more what you're looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}